course: dictionary
lesson: 14932
title: A plan you follow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are used in health and sport, so you may not know them yet. Read the words around them to find the meaning. «The doctor gave Sam a medicine regimen: one tablet every morning for a week.» The clues are tablet, every morning and for a week. A regimen is a plan that tells you what to take or do, and when.
explain: «Mia follows a strict regimen of swimming and healthy food.» Strict tells you the plan has firm rules and must be followed carefully. Try a swap: put "plan" in place of regimen. The sentence still makes sense, so you know the meaning is close.
explain: Some regimens are for training, and some are for getting better after an illness. «Her training regimen included running every day before school.» Both are plans that are done regularly, again and again, not just once.
fact: «Regimen» means a set plan of diet, exercise, medicine or care that someone follows to stay healthy or get better.
fact: In more formal writing, «regimen» can also mean a strict system of rules or routine.
fact: Useful phrases: «a strict regimen», «a training regimen», «a medicine regimen», and «stick to a regimen».
fact: To stick to a regimen means to keep following the plan regularly, even when it is hard.
fact: Regimen is a noun. One is a regimen; more than one is regimens.
exercise: «The doctor gave Sam a medicine regimen.» What is a regimen here? | A game played at break time | A type of bread | A loud noise in the hall | *A set plan of medicine to follow
exercise: Which phrase means keeping to a plan every day? | Count a regimen in fives | Drop a regimen on the floor | *Stick to a regimen | Hide a regimen
exercise: «Mia follows a strict regimen of swimming and healthy food.» What does strict regimen suggest? | A plan that is very short and quick | A plan that was lost in the post | A plan with no rules at all, just for fun | *A plan followed carefully, with firm rules
test: «Her training regimen included running every day before school.» What does training regimen mean? | A school timetable of lessons | *A sport training plan done regularly | A medal for winning a race | A pair of running shoes
test: Which word is closest in meaning to regimen? | *Routine | Puzzle | Holiday | Whistle
exam: Ben says, «A regimen is just a snack.» Is he right? | Yes, it is a bedtime story | No, it is a kind of football | Yes, it is a kind of snack | *No, a regimen is a plan of diet, exercise, medicine or care
